--- a/dxagent/reasoning/belief.py
+++ b/dxagent/reasoning/belief.py
@@ -2,8 +2,13 @@
 
 For every hypothesis d and every observation:
 
-    binary finding f (present / absent):   LLR = log P(obs | d) - log P(obs | background)
-    test t with outcome o:                  LLR = log P(o | d)  - log P(o | background)
+    binary finding f (present / absent):   LLR = log P(report | d) - log P(report | background)
+    test t with outcome o:                  LLR = log P(o | d)      - log P(o | background)
+
+where P(report | d) = r * P(f | d) + (1 - r) * (1 - P(f | d)) with the channel reliability r (a history
+answer is misreported more often than a lab), and a test outcome is replaced by a background draw with
+probability 1 - r. This is the same observation model the planner uses (v0.2.1 fix: v0.2 applied it in
+the planner only, so the belief overweighted noisy reports by about 1.5x).
 
 P(. | d) comes from the disease card (or a contrast card), shrunk toward the background by
 the entry's confidence; diseases with no entry for f use the background, i.e. LLR = 0.
